  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">ABRONET Consortium: Restoring social cohesion among communities affected by violent conflicts in Ethiopia</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Through the Abronet consortium, partners Norwegian Church Aid (NCA), Act Church of Sweden (CoS) and Christian Aid (CA) &#x2013; all members of the ACT Alliance (Action by Churches together), jointly with national partners is initiating a new and innovative collaboration through the project titled; &#x201c;Restoring social cohesion among communities affected by violent conflicts in Ethiopia &#x2013; a religious actors response&#x201d;. The project is mobilising and expanding the capacity of religious actor at community level to engage and mobilise women and men (including youth) in a variety of peacebuilding initiatives to strengthen the unity and social cohesion at community level, both to defuse tensions that are there, but also to prevent future tensions and conflicts that can escalate and threaten the wellbeing of people, stability at community level and ultimately the country and the whole region if left unaddressed. Through the innovative approach and integrating peacebuilding and MHPSS (mental health and psychosocial support) in relation to GBV survivors.</narrative>
  </description>
